"tu.what.t": "What is Hearts?",
"tu.what.b": "A card game for four. Each player gets 13 of the 52 cards, and everyone plays one card at a time.<br>The aim is <b>not to take points</b>: the skill is in steering the point cards to someone else.",
"tu.seats.t": "You and three computer players",
"tu.seats.b": "You sit at the bottom, with {n1} on your left, {n2} across and {n3} on your right.<br>Play goes <b>clockwise</b>: you → {n1} → {n2} → {n3}.",
"tu.hand.t": "Your hand",
"tu.hand.b": "Your cards are sorted by suit: ♣ ♦ ♠ ♥.<br>In every suit <b>the 2 is the lowest and the ace the highest</b>.",
"tu.trick.t": "Tricks",
"tu.trick.b": "One player plays a card (the <b>lead</b>), then each of the others plays one. These four cards are a <b>trick</b>.<br>The highest card of the suit that was led takes the trick, and its player leads next.",
"tu.follow.t": "Follow suit",
"tu.follow.b": "If you have a card of the suit that was led, <b>you must play that suit</b>.<br>Only when you have none may you play any card (a <b>discard</b>). A discard never wins the trick, however high it is.",
"tu.points.t": "The point cards",
"tu.points.b": "In the tricks you take, <b>each heart is 1 point</b> and <b>the Q♠ is 13</b>. Every other card is worth 0.<br>Each hand holds 26 points in all.",
"tu.goal.t": "How to win",
"tu.goal.b": "Points add up hand after hand. When someone reaches <b>100</b>, the game ends,<br>and <b>the player with the fewest points</b> wins.",
"tu.go.t": "Let's play a hand",
"tu.go.b": "Now you play one hand with a fixed deal on the real table.<br>Pick the glowing cards to move on. After each computer card the game stops and explains what happened.",
"tu.pass.t": "First, the pass",
"tu.pass.b": "At the start of a hand you pass <b>3 cards</b> to another player — this time to {n1} on your left.<br>Passing the K♦ and 9♦ leaves you <b>with no diamonds</b>, so you can discard anything when diamonds are led. Let the high A♥ go as well.",
"tu.got.t": "Three cards from the right",
"tu.got.b": "At the same time, {n3} on your right passed you 3 cards (glowing).<br>The direction changes every hand: <b>left → right → across → no pass</b>.",
"tu.c2.t": "The 2♣ starts",
"tu.c2.b": "The first trick is led by <b>whoever holds the 2♣</b>, and it must be that card. This time it is you.",
"tu.n1.t": "{n1} follows with a club",
"tu.n1.b": "{n1} has clubs, so a club it must be: the 10♣.",
"tu.n2.t": "{n2} takes the trick",
"tu.n2.b": "The A♣ is the highest club, so {n2} takes the trick. There is no point card in it: <b>0 points</b>. {n2} leads next.<br>Note: hearts and the Q♠ may not be played on the first trick.",
"tu.p2.t": "Duck with a high card",
"tu.p2.b": "{n2} led the K♣ and {n3} played the 7♣. You must play a club too.<br>Any club below the king will not win. Play <b>the highest of them, the 9♣</b>, and get rid of a card that could cost you later (<b>ducking</b>).",
"tu.n3.t": "{n2} wins again",
"tu.n3.b": "{n1}'s J♣ is below the king as well, so {n2} takes it. No points.",
"tu.p3.t": "Unload the Q♠",
"tu.p3.b": "{n2} led the 5♦ and {n3} played the Q♦. You have <b>no diamonds</b>, so you may play any card.<br>Discard the <b>Q♠</b>: whoever takes this trick gets its 13 points.",
"tu.n4.t": "{n3} gets the Q♠",
"tu.n4.b": "{n1} played the 4♦. The Q♦ is the highest diamond, so {n3} takes the trick <b>with the Q♠: 13 points</b>.<br>That is what passing your diamonds was for.",
"tu.p4.t": "Discard a heart",
"tu.p4.b": "{n3} leads diamonds again (J♦). You still have none, so this time discard a heart: let your highest one, the <b>10♥</b>, go.",
"tu.n5.t": "Hearts are broken",
"tu.n5.b": "{n1} wins with the A♦ and gets the 10♥: <b>1 point</b>.<br>Hearts cannot be led until someone has discarded one. A heart was just discarded (<b>hearts are broken</b>), so from now on hearts may be led.",
"tu.p5.t": "Duck a heart lead",
"tu.p5.b": "{n1} led the 5♥, {n2} played the 7♥ and {n3} the 9♥.<br>Your hearts are 2, 3, 4 and 6 — all below the 9♥, so none of them wins. Play the highest, the <b>6♥</b>.",
"tu.n6.t": "Four hearts for {n3}",
"tu.n6.b": "{n3} wins with the 9♥: <b>4 hearts, 4 points</b>. So far you have 0.<br>The remaining tricks will now be played quickly.",
"tu.e1.t": "The result",
"tu.e1.b": "The points you took are added to your total. This time you have <b>0</b>; {n3}, who took the Q♠, has the most.",
"tu.moon.t": "Shooting the moon",
"tu.moon.b": "If one player takes <b>all 13 hearts and the Q♠</b>, that player scores 0 and <b>the other three get 26 each</b>.<br>A bold plan — but miss a single card and you take a pile of points. If someone seems to be going for it, take one heart to stop them.",
"tu.vars.t": "Other rules",
"tu.vars.b": "You can choose a variant under New.<br><b>Omnibus</b>: taking the J♦ is −10.<br><b>Black Maria</b>: the K♠ is 10 and the A♠ 7 as well.<br><b>Spot Hearts</b>: hearts score their face value.",
"tu.coach.t": "Coach and hint",
"tu.coach.b": "While you play, the <b>coach</b> on the right (a tab below on phones) shows the card it suggests, why, and the points each card is likely to cost.<br>If you are stuck, the <b>Hint</b> button picks the suggested card.",
"tu.study.t": "Counting, review and study",
"tu.study.b": "<b>Counting</b> shows the cards not yet played and who is out of which suit.<br><b>Review</b> opens everyone's hand and replays the hand card by card; <b>Study</b> works out passes and expected points.",
"tu.learn.t": "Practising more",
"tu.learn.b": "<b>Lessons</b>: practise ducking, discards, passing, stopping the moon and more with problems.<br><b>Rules</b>: the rules and a glossary. You can also replay this tutorial from Rules.",
"tu.end.t": "Tutorial complete",
"tu.end.b": "That covers the basics of Hearts.<br>Start with weaker computer players (Lv.1–5) and keep an eye on the coach as you play.",
